</year><publisher-name>NY &#x00026; London: The Guilford Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nardi</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name><name><surname>Whittaker</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Hinds P, Kiesler S</surname></name></person-group><article-title>The Place of Face-to-Face Communication in Distributed Work</article-title><source>Distributed Work</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>Cambridge: The MIT Press</publisher-name><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>110</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boix-Mansilla</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardner</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><source>Assessing interdisciplinary work at the frontier: An empirical exploration of "symptoms of quality</source><year>2004</year><publisher-name>GoodWork Project Website Research Paper</publisher-name><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.goodwork.org"/></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Klein</surname><given-names>JT</given-names></name></person-group><source>Interdisciplinarity: History, Theory, and Practice</source><year>1990</year><publisher-name>Detroit: Wayne State University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B22"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Moran</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><source>Interdisciplinarity</source><year>2002</year><publisher-name>London: Routledge</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nowotny</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name>